From 86331f2377317798cc6690ac9667ecb0acc09a34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelinek <jakub@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:30:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] testsuite: Fix up sso-22.c test

The new gcc.dg/sso-22.c test FAILs on i686-linux:
FAIL: gcc.dg/sso-22.c (test for excess errors)
Excess errors:
/home/jakub/src/gcc/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/sso-22.c:19:8: error: invalid conversion to type '_Float16' without option '-msse2'
/home/jakub/src/gcc/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/sso-22.c:23:11: error: operation not permitted on type '_Float16' without option '-msse2'
All tests which require float16 effective target should also have
corresponding dg-add-options float16 which arranges to add options
needed for that, but this one didn't have it.

2026-11-25  Jakub Jelinek  <jakub@redhat.com>

	* gcc.dg/sso-22.c: Add dg-add-options float16 directive.
---
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/sso-22.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/sso-22.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/sso-22.c
index 1633348415f8..08078c24cd6c 100644
--- a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/sso-22.c
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/sso-22.c
@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@
 /* PR debug/128920 */
-
 /* { dg-do run } */
 /* { dg-options "-std=c23" }
 /* { dg-require-effective-target float16 } */
+/* { dg-add-options float16 } */
 
 #if __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_LITTLE_ENDIAN__
 struct __attribute__((scalar_storage_order("big-endian"))) S
